{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the summary.\n\n## The table\nThe note's bounds were slightly off. On the fixed 6-byte grid (each row = 3 pairs = one 2×3 sprite form), the enemy sprite layout table actually runs **prgRom 0x673E–0x683F** (CPU $E73E–$E83F), **43 rows × 6 bytes = 258 bytes** — the note's 0x6744 start was one row late and 0x683D two bytes short. At **0x6840** a *separate* 27-byte table begins, the per-graphics-type offset table read by `LDA $E840,Y` (CPU $E92A); every entry is a row offset/6, and type 6 → 0x54 → the Goomba row I confirmed. The reader is CPU $EBAA (`LDA $E73E,X / LDA $E73F,X / JMP $F282`), which draws one 2×2 per call with X stepping by 2.\n\nRecorded with `record_mapping` (note `enemy sprite layout rows`, confidence 1, rom_origins prgRom 0x673E length 0x102) listing all 43 rows, e.g.:\n- 0x673E = FC FC AA AB AC AD = Buzzy Beetle\n- 0x674A = FC A5 A6 A7 A8 A9 = Koopa Troopa walk (tiles match the mapping's live Koopa)\n- 0x6792 = FC FC 70 71 72 73 = Goomba\n- 0x67C8 = FC FC FC FC EF EF = the flattened/stomped form\n- First row **0x673E**, last row **0x683A** (F0 F0 + four blanks — an 8×16 fragment, where rows stop being full enemy frames)\n\n## The proof\n- `new_hack eval-sheet2-rows-b` (\"eval run\") and `use_hack` it.\n- Ledgered `write_memory` prgRom **0x6792** with the Koopa row `FC A5 A6 A7 A8 A9`.\n- `reset_emulator`, played Start/Start and walked Right to 1-1's first Goomba.\n- **list_sprites** decoded the enemy as tiles `$A5,$FC,$A7,$A6,$A9,$A8` (was `$FC,$FC,$70,$71,$72,$73`), and the screenshot shows the enemy on the hill drawn with the Koopa's form (palette 7 still, since the palette comes from the type). This proves the row at 0x6792 selects the drawn sprite.\n- `undo_edit` seq 1 restored `FC FC 70 71 72 73`; `use_hack default`.\n\n`promote_mappings` was called once at the end (1 discovery promoted; the earlier 0.6 hypothesis was skipped).\n\nOne honest caveat: the mid-table rows are solid (Goomba, Koopa, stomp row are confirmed), but the small effect/object rows at the tail (0x6828–0x683A) are shape-based best guesses; the notes flag them. The visual-naming subagent I spawned failed without output, so those come from my own view_tiles pass."}
